 "blind": true,
 "statement": "Annotated blind from the Beinecke scan only (canvas 1006200, labelled '70v (part)'; the one of the two '70v (part)' canvases whose ring counts, 19 outer figures, 10 inner figures and one central scene, match the label-line structure of f70v2: label lines .2-.20, .22-.31 and .33 between circular text lines .1, .21, .32). Three rings: an outer ring of 19 bare-breasted female figures emerging from patterned tubs or garments, each with a star (six of them, at 12 to 4 o'clock, wear blue caps); an inner ring of 10 nude female figures with tubs, most tubs tinted green, each with a star; a centre disc with two cross-hatched fish facing opposite ways above a blue-edged curved line, plus two eight-pointed stars. Every figure has a short written label beside it on the scan, but no label line id is assigned to any figure: the label line ids carry no position, and tying an id to a figure would mean reading the label words in the transcription, which a blind annotation must not do. Each figure instead carries its ring, clock position and clockwise order, and the label line ids of its ring as candidates; a scorer or second annotator who knows where ZL starts each ring's numbering can map order to id. The centre has words beside the upper star and between the fish; which of them is f70v2.33 cannot be told blind.",
